    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95955" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπλαγχν-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>eat the inwards</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπλάγχνα</span>) <i>of a victim</i> after a sacrifice, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				984
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				37.30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Doroth.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				9.410b
			</span></i>; dub. sens. and constr. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				4.4.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσπλαγχνευμένων τῶν ἱερῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					1.40
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>prophesy from the inwards</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπλαγχνοσκοπία</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				7.2.3
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.3.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.27
			</span></i>.</div>
